WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.590
Film Courage: Here is the look at yourself
in the mirror question “Are you really ready?”

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.530
What are some tough questions that you have
to ask yourself?

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:07.930
Because we all think we’re ready.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:13.160
We wouldn’t come here or we wouldn’t (whether
we grew up here or not) try to do something

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.920
where we don’t think…our ego thinks we’re
ready…but maybe we’re not.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:17.920
How do we know?

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.910
Author Carole Kirschner: That’s a really
good question, how do you know?

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:30.730
You know if you’re getting the kind of responses
that you’re looking for, if people are interested

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:38.460
in you, if people want to help you, if doors
are opening for you.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:47.280
If your material (again, if you’re a writer)
is blazing hot, not “this is like a really

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.280
good draft.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.280
I’m going to do another one.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.130
But I’m going to send out this one because
it’s really good.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.550
I can do better, but this is really good.”

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.579
You have one shot.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:01.989
So if your material isn’t there yet…I
know very smart people who have fantastic

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:07.679
connections, but they are not sending out
their material until they know that it’s

00:01:07.679 --> 00:01:08.679
great.

00:01:08.679 --> 00:01:10.560
Until they know that it’s blazing hot.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:17.250
So if you’re not getting people who want
to help you, people who want to open some

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:23.799
doors for you, if you’re not getting positive
responses, then you’re probably not ready

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:24.799
yet.

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:29.149
Film Courage: Okay, let’s take a little
bit of a twist, let’s suppose you are getting

00:01:29.149 --> 00:01:33.749
all of these green lights from people but
there is something in you sabotaging it.

00:01:33.749 --> 00:01:34.749
Carole Kirschner: Oh…yes.

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:36.429
Film Courage: Do you see this a lot?

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.270
Carole Kirschner: I have seen it.

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:39.400
I’ve absolutely seen it.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:44.649
In my book I talk about a young woman and
it was really sad.

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:46.399
She was a waitress in Malibu.

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:52.709
She was an aspiring actress and her idol came
into the restaurant where she worked and she

00:01:52.709 --> 00:01:57.909
happened to be in her section and this young
woman struck up a conversation with her idol.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:01:59.559
And her idol said “What do you do?”

00:01:59.559 --> 00:02:01.579
And she said said “I’m an aspiring actress.”

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:04.290
And her idol said “Well, you know what?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:09.569
I’m shooting in Los Angeles, why don’t
you come and visit the set tomorrow?”

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:12.099
And the waitress said “Oh my God!

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:13.340
That would be amazing.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.349
Thank you so much!”

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:16.819
She was so excited.

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:19.310
She went out with her friends the night before.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.379
She drank too much.

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:25.939
She set her alarm clock but not for the right
time.

00:02:25.939 --> 00:02:27.849
She woke up hungover.

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:30.379
She woke up too late.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:35.680
And she totally sabotaged herself because
emotionally she wasn’t ready for it.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.969
And it’s heartbreaking when you see that.

00:02:38.969 --> 00:02:44.540
Film Courage: What are some things that you
see…I mean that’s a great example.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.930
I’ve seen people who have done stuff like
that.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.620
I think that it’s because they are scared
but they don’t want to admit it.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.590
What are some of the things that you can see
like….ahhh…that’s the sabotage sort

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.120
of veil working there.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:00.760
Carole Kirschner: Sure, let me think about
that.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:10.030
I think if somebody is being obnoxious or
too pushy, that is certainly a way to sabotage

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.400
yourself.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.659
If your material isn’t ready and you’re
sending it out.

00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:25.019
And another way to sabotage yourself is everybody
is on social media all the time.

00:03:25.019 --> 00:03:33.519
If your digital profile is not professional,
that’s a way to sabotage yourself.

00:03:33.519 --> 00:03:39.060
I once was looking to hire an assistant and
this woman had a great resume, but I looked

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:46.049
on her Facebook page and her profile picture
was her, at a party, with her sleeve kind

00:03:46.049 --> 00:03:47.639
of off, holding a red cup.

00:03:47.639 --> 00:03:51.129
And I thought I can’t hire this woman?

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:57.019
And she had a great resume but I wouldn’t
hire her because she wasn’t professional

00:03:57.019 --> 00:04:00.219
and she didn’t have common sense that you
don’t do that.

00:04:00.219 --> 00:04:06.810
Let me think of what else it might be…when
you don’t deliver on what you say you’re

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.810
going to do.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.000
That is a huge thing.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.900
If you make promises that you can’t keep,
that’s totally sabotaging yourself.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.639
It’s better to oversell and underdeliver.

